[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888434811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106523#issuecomment-2888434811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106523","id":2888434811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sKgR7","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T14:42:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T15:16:24Z","body":"It does appear (at least pre-2022) that MSVC compiler might not be so good at optimizing `if else` compared to `switch`.\r\n\r\nFirst question though - have you got some profiles indicating this to be a bottleneck in real world (or benchmark) cases?\r\nWe usually prefer to limit micro-optimization to cases where there's evidence of a bottleneck.\r\n\r\n(Culling can be, so it could well be useful, but it would be nice to confirm this either way. :+1: )","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888434811/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888485757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106523#issuecomment-2888485757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106523","id":2888485757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sKst9","user":{"login":"nukethebees","id":4354670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ2NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4354670?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees","html_url":"https://github.com/nukethebees","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nukethebees/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T16:39:33Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T16:39:33Z","body":"I profiled it with the official culling benchmarks and it doesn't make any measurable difference as most of the time is spent in a much larger conditional earlier in the function.\n\nYou may as well close this then I guess. \n\nIs there a threshold for what's considered a sufficient improvement?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888485757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888502474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106523#issuecomment-2888502474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106523","id":2888502474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sKwzK","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T17:23:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T17:23:48Z","body":"> Is there a threshold for what's considered a sufficient improvement?\r\n\r\nThere's no hard rules, but generally for optimization only PRs we like to see things make a significant improvement in benchmarks (i.e. measureable), and more so for ones that may make code more difficult to read - there is a trade off here, as optimizations often make less readable code, and often less easily maintainable code.\r\n\r\nSee https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/general_optimization.html#principles\r\n\r\nGenerally it is advisable for optimization PRs (CPU) to:\r\n\r\n1) Find a slow project / benchmark\r\n2) Profile\r\n3) Optimize bottleneck\r\n\r\nThis avoids wasting development / review time on areas which will not improve things.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888502474/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888631721","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106523#issuecomment-2888631721","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106523","id":2888631721,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sLQWp","user":{"login":"jss2a98aj","id":11281893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjgxODkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11281893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj","html_url":"https://github.com/jss2a98aj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jss2a98aj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T23:14:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T23:14:07Z","body":"I do find this to be an improvement to readability even if the performance impact is negligible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888631721/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket